      "text": "Let the four positive integers be $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and $d$. We know that when these integers are divided by $11$, they leave remainders of $2,$ $4,$ $6,$ and $8$, respectively. This can be expressed as:\n\\[\na \\equiv 2 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nb \\equiv 4 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nc \\equiv 6 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\\[\nd \\equiv 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nTo find the remainder when $a + b + c + d$ is divided by $11$, we first compute the sum $a + b + c + d$:\n\\[\na + b + c + d \\equiv 2 + 4 + 6 + 8 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the sum of $2 + 4 + 6 + 8$:\n\\[\n2 + 4 + 6 + 8 = 20\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the remainder when $20$ is divided by $11$:\n\\[\n20 \\div 11 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 9\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\n20 \\equiv 9 \\pmod{11}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum of the four integers is divided by $11$ is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{9}\n\\]",
